summary: Fedora SELinux tier1 tests on MLS (COPR selinux-policy-mls)
description: |
    Switch the guest to MLS with prepare_for_mls (RHEL MLS switch:
    permissive, fixfiles -F onboot, reboot, then enforcing), install
    selinux-policy-mls from COPR, then run Fedora package SELinux tier1
    integration tests from https://src.fedoraproject.org/tests/selinux.git
    (same filter as /tier1-filtered: tier:1, exclude failinfedora and epel).

    Env: COPR_REPO (required in CI); optional COPR_SELINUX_POLICY_MLS_NVR.

prepare:
  - name: COPR MLS policy and guest switch
    how: shell
    script: $TMT_TREE/tmt/mls-copr-prepare.sh

discover:
  - name: fedora-selinux-tier1
    how: fmf
    url: https://src.fedoraproject.org/tests/selinux.git
    filter: "tier:1 & tag:-failinfedora & tag:-epel"

execute:
  how: tmt
